{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358282-white-elephant-for-epee102-the-lotus-of-enlightenment-2cd","id":1358282,"title":"[White Elephant for Epee102] The Lotus of Enlightenment [2CD]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-01T15:41:53-08:00","id":1358282,"title":"[White Elephant for Epee102] The Lotus of Enlightenment [2CD]","content":"Merry Belated Christmas <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11835_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11835\" data-vbnamecard=\"11835\">Epee102</a>! Hope you enjoy!<br /> <br /> Those who attempt to summit the slopes of Qaf may find themselves in the presence of a strangely beautiful marble-skinned woman, dressed in the finest silks and sitting atop a giant flying amaranthine Lotus flower. She will usually offer the supplicants of the Heaven Violating Spear a koan or proverb to aid them on their road to enlightenment. Those who internalize her advice and advance up the slopes as a result will be lifted up to a grand barque of flower-petals, floating ever up the slopes of Qaf evermore.<br /> <br /> The woman is Sadaya, the Lotus of Enlightenment, the Expressive Soul of Kratu, the Ship of Knowledge, 5th Soul of the Heaven Violating Spear. Above all else, Kratu seeks to reach the summit of his greater-self. Ages ago he learned that, through carrying with him other enlightened souls, he could increase her own speed towards the summit. Since then, he set his second-circle souls about finding enough enlightened ones to crew his ship-self with sufficient speed to sail unto infinity. <br /> <br /> Trapped as she is in the domains of Hell, Sadaya\u2019s pickings on this front are somewhat limited, mostly restricted to those oddest of demons who have elected to walk the slopes of Qaf. In this manner, she has cultivated an unintended rivalry with Zeno, the Road to Infinity. Zeno takes pleasure in stopping those he deems unworthy of enlightenment from climbing Qaf by trapping them in his own infinite roadways, but Sadaya will offer those trapped within Zeno\u2019s roads the same test as she does all others, and will rescue them if they succeed. Zeno has more than once attempted to punish Sadaya for her interference in his affairs, but has always failed in his attempts to imprison her. <br /> <br /> Sadaya is most fond of what few opportunities she has to collect souls from Creation. If a mortal meditates for a full week with neither sleep, food, nor water atop a pillar of stone or a mountain summit, Sadaya may slip into Creation. Her time there is limited, as she has no more than an hour before she is drawn back into Hell. More often than not, she quizzes those who managed to call her into the world to see if they are worthy of voyage to enlightenment, and if so, convince them to join her on Qaf. Those who fail to meet her standards are rendered mute, lest they spread their \u2018tainted\u2019 philosophy to others. Those few who far surpass Sadaya\u2019s standards, instead of recruiting directly, she convinces to open schools of philosophy and ascetic monasteries in hopes that they will spread their knowledge to others and grant her an even greater harvest of \u2018recruits\u2019. To this end, Sadaya teaches them a mystic art as demonstration of the power of their enlightenment. Some small handful may learn a martial art, or take the first steps towards the mastery of sorcery, but most Sadaya teaches a Thaumaturgical ritual or sutra that offers a visually impressive display, such as the ability to breathe fire or float. <br /> <br /> Sadaya is herself quite fond of the Immaculate faiths, as their own ascetic traditions have given her more than a few opportunities to enter Creation. Their preference for vegetarianism also strikes a chord with the demon, as she finds the practice of killing to be utterly repugnant. There are few cases in which Sadaya finds lethal violence acceptable, and all those involved in the preservation of knowledge or saving some soul that she believes to be enlightened grievous harm. This is not to say that she is a friend to human life, however. Sadaya\u2019s own brand of enlightenment is one of extreme, almost neglectful, asceticism in favor of cultivating the mind and soul. While perfectly health for her and many other spirits, this has lead more than a few of her human supplicants to die of starvation or exposure while in pursuit of her teachings. She also has a fiery temper, and has been known to kill those who have rejected or strayed from her teachings, lest they draw others away from the road to enlightenment.<br /> <br /> <b>Sadaya, the Lotus of Enlightenment, Expressive Soul of the Ship of Knowledge</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Intimacies:<br /> Defining Principle: I will draw all into perfect enlightenment<br /> Major Principle: Rejection of enlightenment is tantamount to suicide <br /> Major Tie: Kratu (Enlightened master)<br /> Major Principle: Life should be preserved; killing is for the crude and unenlightened<br /> Minor tie: Philosophers (respect)<br /> <br /> Essence: 6; Willpower: 8; Join Battle: 9 dice<br /> Personal Motes: 100<br /> Health Levels: -0x2/-1x4/-2x6/-4x2/Incap <br /> Actions: Demonic Lore: 8 Dice; Read Intentions: 12 Dice; Philosophy: 13 dice; Senses: 9 dice; Social Influence: 12 Dice; <br /> Appearance 6, Resolve 6, Guile 5<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Cult 1<br /> <br /> Martial Artist: Sadaya is a master of the Crane and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Styles of Martial Arts, learned from a Sidereal lover in the early days of the first age who shared many of her views on how to perfect the soul. Her garb qualifies to fit all practical requirements for both style\u2019s charms. <br /> <br /> Combat<br /> Attack (Unarmed): 14 Dice (Damage 12)<br /> Attack (Grapple): 12 Dice (Control: 10 dice)<br /> <br /> Combat Movement: 9 dice<br /> Evasion 4, Parry 5<br /> Soak/Hardness: 12/0<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> Combat<br /> Coiling Roots of the Perfected Lotus- (5m; Reflexive; Instant; Decisive-only, Clash) Sadaya\u2019s lotus flower is a part of her being; all parts of it are at her command, and a mighty tool for her defense. The roots unfurl, coiling and ensnaring all who dare to strike at such a holy teacher. Sadaya may activate this charm in response to any attack that targets her at close range, making an unarmed attack as a clash. If Sadaya wins the clash, then her opponent is immediately Grappled. Sadaya may ensnare up to 6 individuals in grapples at a time, but must also pay 5m per combat round to maintain the grapples. If she does not, all opponents are immediately released. If she does, she may choose to independently savage, restrain or throw, or release any of her grappled targets. <br /> <br /> Social Charms<br /> Fruit of Enlightenment- (2m; Supplemental, Instant): Should a pupil wish to remain in ignorance, a good teacher only redoubles their efforts to lead them down the path to knowledge. This charm supplements an Instill or Persuade action, converting one of Sadaya\u2019s dice to an automatic success for every bonus point the target receives to their resolve from applicable intimacies. <br /> <br /> Miscellaneous Charms:<br /> Hurry Home (10m, 1wp; Simple; Instant) Sadaya may activate this charm to immediately return to Kratu, the Ship of Knowledge or her Summoner, if applicable. <br /> <br /> Materialize (50m, 1wp; Simple; Instant)<br /> <br /> Measure the Wind (5m; Simple; Instant) Sadaya may activate this charm on anyone who engages in philosophical discussion with her. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T21:05:16-08:00","id":1358345,"title":"","content":"This is very cool, and I'm guessing she's not terribly fond of Suntarankal.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's not so harsh between them -- they clearly have different teaching styles, but they're both quite capable of being harsh in their own ways, and they both do their best to bring their students to enlightenment.<br /> <br /> (I had an idea a while back, that infernal martial artists would spar on the slopes of Qaf, trying to seek enlightenment and get the advantage over their opponent. For some reason, I hadn't thought about subsidiary souls of Qaf that might be hanging around.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T02:59:17-08:00","id":1358383,"title":"","content":"Ah, more love for my favorite Yozi that lives! This is awesome! Permission to reference her in my STV material? And her diamond vessel over soul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T11:11:48-08:00","id":1358452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358282-white-elephant-for-epee102-the-lotus-of-enlightenment-2cd?p=1358383#post1358383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, more love for my favorite Yozi that lives! This is awesome! Permission to reference her in my STV material? And her diamond vessel over soul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like her! Qaf is my favorite Yozi too, and he definitely needs more literary love. <br /> <br /> And permission granted!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T11:28:39-08:00","id":1358454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358282-white-elephant-for-epee102-the-lotus-of-enlightenment-2cd?p=1358345#post1358345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is very cool, and I'm guessing she's not terribly fond of Suntarankal.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it's not so harsh between them -- they clearly have different teaching styles, but they're both quite capable of being harsh in their own ways, and they both do their best to bring their students to enlightenment.<br /> <br /> (I had an idea a while back, that infernal martial artists would spar on the slopes of Qaf, trying to seek enlightenment and get the advantage over their opponent. For some reason, I hadn't thought about subsidiary souls of Qaf that might be hanging around.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm, I hadn\u2019t considered what her feelings on Sunturankal would be...<br /> <br /> I think she would have antagonistic relationship with him. The Crucible of Brass and Iron teaches Martial Arts as a means of developing strength and spreading Isadoros\u2019 might-makes-right philosophy, while Sadaya teaches martial arts as a means for the practitioner to gain control over their bodies and the worldly desires that come with. The two have almost diametrically opposed philosophies, and if there\u2019s one thing that makes Sadaya livid it\u2019s people pushing radically different philosophies about what constitutes enlightenment. I could very well see her just declaring that anyone who bears the 19-spined eye marking them as a graduate of Sunturankal as a lost cause and killing them on sight. <br /> <br /> That infernal martial arts meet is an awesome idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:13:03-08:00","id":1358527,"title":"","content":"Of course, one could argue that the <i>proper</i> way for two sifus to square off is to pit their students against each other.<br /> <br /> Just as Peleps Deled proves the accuracy of his view of the Immaculate texts by beating other monks to death, demonic martial artists can demonstrate the superiority of their sifu's philosophy by killing each other.<br /> <br /> Possibly on the slopes of Qaf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:33:16-08:00","id":1358531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358282-white-elephant-for-epee102-the-lotus-of-enlightenment-2cd?p=1358527#post1358527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....Possibly on the slopes of Qaf.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Zeno laughing intensifies]<br /> <br /> In less memey terms, I quite approve of this new addition to Qaf's soul hierarchy. I'm also highly amused how this directly references our chronicle notes. Bravo, Sir. Great work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}